2.THE LCCP hereby agrees to:
a.Monitor and evaluate the City's compliance with the terms of this Contract.
b.Monitor the performance of the City's program, including fiscal management, and all
other data detailed inwritten reports and sitevisits; and
c.Provide technical assistance and training to the City.
3.COMPENSATION.LCCP agrees to pay the City an amount not to exceed One Hundred and
Twenty Eight Thousand, Five Hundred Dollars ($128,500)for the performance of the above
services.The City willinvoice LCCP in accordance with the City's prepared budget and
Wyoming Department of Education requirements, as defined in the Wyoming 21st Centoy
Com mum it y Learning Centers 2013-2018Grant Application, Attachment A.LCCP shallnot
be required to pay any invoice unless and until it receives the funds applied for from the
Department.Payment for reimbursement will made within thirty (30) days of receipt of each
invoice issued by the City.
4.TERM. The term of this Contract shall commence on the 1 day of May 2013 and terminate
on the 30th day of April, 2014, unless terminated earlier as set forth in paragraph seven (7) of
this Contract.
5.CITY'S CONTACT PERSON.Dick Berry, Directorof Cheyenne Office of Youth
Alternatives,1328Talbot Court, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
6.PROOF OF INSURANCE.City provides liability coverage in accordance with the Wyoming
G over m mental Claims Act(WGCA).A certification of such coverage willbe provided to
LCCP.
7.TERMINATION.If, through any cause, the City shall fail to fulfill in a timely and proper
manner, its obligations under this Contract; or if the City violates any of the covenants,
agreements, or stipulations of the Contract; LCCPmay terminate this Contract if such default
or violation is not correction within thirty (30) days following City's receipt of any notice of
a violation issued byLCCP.
