10.FEDERAL AUDIT REQUIREMENTS. Each party understands that if more than five-
hundred-thousand dollars ($500, o00) in federal funds from all sources are expended, the
parties are required toconduct a single-audit as requiredby Office of Management &
Budget(OMB)CircularA-133.
11. CONFIDENTIALITY. Nothing in this Contract shall be deemed to require the parties to
release any information that is considered confidential by state or federal law.
12. INDEMNIFICATION. Each party agrees to be responsible for any losses, claims, damages,
injuries, demands and causes of action resulting from that party's negligence.The City does
hereby reserve all immunities and defenses provided under the WGCA.
13. CERTIFICATION REGARDING DISBARMENT AND SUSPENSION. By signing this
Contract, the City certifies to the best of its knowledge and belief that it and its principles are
not presently debarred, suspended, proposedfor debarment, declared ineligible, or voluntarily
excluded from participation in this transaction by any federal department or agency.
14. EQUIPMENT.If the City uses grant funds under this Contract to purchase any piece
equipment and the Contract is terminated forbreach, the piece of cquipment shall be returned
to the LCCP within thirty (30) days following termination of this Contract. All purchases
remain property ofLCCP and return may be requested.
